#. +> trunk
msgctxt "NAME OF TRANSLATORS"
msgid "Your names"
msgstr "Manfred Wiese"

#. +> trunk
msgctxt "EMAIL OF TRANSLATORS"
msgid "Your emails"
msgstr "m.j.wiese@web.de"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that if a book has more than one author, you should separate\n"
"their names by a semi-colon, so that Tellico will know how to split them\n"
"and use them separately.</p>"
"\n"
"<p>Any other field which allows multiple values should be entered the\n"
"same way, with a semi-colon (;) separating each value.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du Autorennaams mit Streekpünkt scheden schullst, wenn\n"
"een Book mehr as een Autor hett, dormit Tellico weet, wodennig de\n"
"to scheden sünd un de ok enkelt bruken kann.</p>"
"\n"
"<p>Weerten mööt ok binnen all anner Feller, de mehr Weerten verlöövt, mit Streekpünkt (;) scheedt warrn.</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can change which fields are shown in the list view by\n"
"right-clicking on the column header.\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du de wiest Feller in de Listansicht ännern kannst, wenn Du mit de Muus en Rechtsklick op den Strieptitel maakst?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can add, edit, or modify the fields in the collection using\n"
"the Field Editor. The arrow buttons below the field list can be used to change the\n"
"position of the field in the list, which affects the placement in the entry\n"
"editor.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du Feller binnen de Sammeln mit den Feldeditor tofögen, bewerken\n"
"oder ännern kannst? Mit de Pielknööp nerrn de Feldlist laat sik Indrääg\n"
"in de List verschuven. Dat ännert de Positschoon in'n Indrageditor.</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that if you want to filter by a Checkbox field, a value of\n"
"\"true\" should be used. If you'd like to filter to\n"
"show only the science fiction books which you've not read, for\n"
"example, check the <em>Match all of the\n"
"following</em> button,  set the first rule to have \"Genre\"\n"
"\"contains\" \"Science Fiction\" (no quotes) and the second rule to\n"
"have \"Read\" \"does not contain\" \"true\" (no quotes).</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du den Weert \"true\" bruken schullst, wenn Du na en\n"
"Krüüzfeld filterst? Wenn Du a.B. bloots de Sciencefiction-Böker\n"
"wiesen wullt, de Du noch nich leest hest, maak <em>Passt op all Nakamen</em>\n"
"an, legg as eerste Regel \"Oort\" fast, \"bargt\" \"Sciencefiction\"\n"
"(ahn Goosfööt) un as twete Regel \"Leest\" \"bargt nich\" \"true\"\n"
"(ahn Goosfööt).</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that if a non-word character is used in the Quick Filter, the text is\n"
"interpreted as a regular expression.</p>"
"\n"
"<p>To show only books which are by Weber or Bujold, for example, then\n"
"type \"weber|bujold\" (no quotes) in the filter box.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat bi Bruuk vun en Nich-Textteken in'n Fixfilter de Text as\n"
"reguleer Utdruck düüdt warrt?.</p>"
"\n"
"<p> Wenn Du a.B. bloots Böker wiesen wullt, de Harte oder Sass schreven\n"
"hebbt, giff in't Filterfeld \"harte|sass\" (ahn Goosfööt) in.</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can edit more than one entry at a time, by holding down\n"
"the Shift or Ctrl key and selecting multiple entries.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du mehr as een Indrag op eenmaal bewerken kannst, wenn Du de\n"
"Ümschalt- oder Strg-Tast daaldrückt höllst un mehr Indrääg utsöchst?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can convert an existing book collection to a bibliography,\n"
"which can then be exported to bibtex or Bibtexml format.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>... dat Du en vörhannen Bökersammeln na en Bökerverteken ümwanneln\n"
"kannst, dat sik denn na't Bibtex- oder Bibtexml-Formaat exporteren lett?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can add, edit, and delete string macros for bibliographies.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>... dat Du Tekenkedenmakros för Bökervertekens tofögen, bewerken, oder wegmaken kannst?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that if more than one field is formatted as a name, then an additional\n"
"group named \"People\" is added to the collection, allowing authors and editors\n"
"to be sorted or printed together, for example.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat de Sammeln en Bito-Koppel mit den Naam \"Lüü\" toföögt warrt,\n"
"wenn mehr as een Feld as Naam formateert is, so dat sik a.B.\n"
"Schrievers un Bewerkers tohoop sorteren oder drucken laat?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can modify the appearance of the printed output by modifying\n"
"the <tt>tellico-printing.xsl</tt> file. The file generates HTML, and the CSS\n"
"within the stylesheet governs things like the font, the margins, etc.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du dat Druckutsehn ännern kannst, wenn Du de Datei\n"
"<tt>tellico-printing.xsl</tt> ännerst? De Datei stellt HTML op, un mit de\n"
"CSS-Stilvörlaag warrt a.B. Schriftoort, Ränners, usw. stüert.</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can import using any generic XSL stylesheet which\n"
"outputs a valid Tellico XML file.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>... dat Du för't Importeren all allmeen XSL-Stilvörlagen\n"
"bruken kannst, de gellen XML-Dateien för Tellico utgeevt?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that double-clicking an entry item opens the Entry Editor.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>... dat sik mit en Dubbelklick op en Indrag de Indrag-Editor opmaken lett?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can add HTML tags to any Paragraph field for formatting, such as\n"
"&lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt; or &lt;i&gt;italic&lt;/i&gt;.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>... dat sik HTML-Betekers för't Formateren vun Afsnittfeller tofögen laat, a.B.:\n"
"&lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt; oder &lt;i&gt;italic&lt;/i&gt;.</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that in the Detailed View, you can press a letter on the\n"
"keyboard to skip to the next entry that starts with that letter.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat Du in de Enkelheiten-Ansicht en Bookstaventast drücken kannst,\n"
"un so na den Indrag jumpen kannst, de mit den Bookstaav anfangt?</p>"
"\n"

#. +> trunk
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can use a field with a derived value to combine multiple separated fields\n"
"into a single field. Use a derived value template\n"
"similar to \"Value: %{fielda}%{fieldb}\" where %{...} gets replaced with the\n"
"appropriate field value. This is useful to collect multiple values in a\n"
"single field, e.g. for better grouping, and to combine fields of different\n"
"types by respecting proper sorting at the same time. Consider for example\n"
"a number field followed by a text subfield with entries 3b, 14a.</p>"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"<p>...dat sik mit afleddt Weerten mehr enkelte Feller binnen een Feld tosamenfaten laat?\n"
"Bruuk en Vörlaag mit afleddt Weerten, so as \"Weert: %{feld_a}%{feld_b}\". För \"%{...}\"\n"
"warrt de tohören Feldweert inföögt.  Dit is goot för't Tosamenfaten vun mehr Weerten\n"
"binnen een Feld, a.B. för beter Tohoopkoppeln un för't Tosamenfaten vun mehr verscheden\n"
"Feldtypen, bides de liekers propper sorteert warrt. En Bispill: en Tallenfeld mit nakamen\n"
"Textünnerfeld, mit de Indrääg 3b un 14a.</p>"
"\n"

